# LFP Accounting — pull every 15 minutes
# Install with: crontab -e   (then paste this line)
# Cron is started automatically by the Pi at boot, so this survives reboots.
#
# This is the ACTIVE mechanism on the production Pi (the systemd unit/timer
# in this folder are an unused alternative). Adjust the path, --printer IP,
# and interval to match your install.
#
# pull.log is gitignored and grows over time; to cap it, rotate with logrotate
# or periodically truncate (e.g. a weekly `: > pull.log` cron entry).
#
# The printer serial (needed to decrypt per-job ink) is hardcoded in
# lfp_accounting.py (DEFAULT_PRINTER_SERIAL), so nothing extra is needed here.
# Only if the printer is ever replaced, prepend LFP_PRINTER_SERIAL=<new-serial>
# to override it.

*/15 * * * * cd /home/gbgbild/gbgbild-accounting && /usr/bin/python3 lfp_accounting.py --printer 192.168.1.55 pull >> /home/gbgbild/gbgbild-accounting/pull.log 2>&1

# Monthly billing — send the PREVIOUS month's jobs to the shop endpoint.
# Runs 06:00 on days 1-7. send-batch with no date args defaults to the previous
# calendar month; it is idempotent (marks jobs sent), so day 1 sends and days 2-7
# are no-ops ("No sendable jobs"). The 1-7 window auto-retries a failed 1st, so a
# network/endpoint blip on the 1st doesn't silently skip a month's billing.
# Requires the Bearer token in ~/.lfp_accounting/token (cron has no exported env).
0 6 1-7 * * cd /home/gbgbild/gbgbild-accounting && /usr/bin/python3 lfp_accounting.py send-batch >> /home/gbgbild/gbgbild-accounting/send-batch.log 2>&1
